{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14240563,"type":"Lesson","status":"Processed","importance":2,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":7,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":9,"pointsAwarded":9,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-15T11:57:53.000Z","started":"2026-10-15T12:21:20.000Z","completed":"2026-10-15T12:22:39.000Z","processed":"2026-10-15T12:22:51.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62260242,"studentId":57975,"choices":null,"selectedChoice":1,"selectId":0,"correct":1,"timeElapsed":13891,"question":{"id":44935,"exampleId":14378,"difficulty":1}},{"id":62260270,"studentId":57975,"choices":null,"selectedChoice":null,"selectId":0,"correct":1,"timeElapsed":10111,"question":{"id":215884,"exampleId":14378,"difficulty":3}},{"id":62260317,"studentId":57975,"choices":null,"selectedChoice":1,"selectId":0,"correct":1,"timeElapsed":15944,"question":{"id":67194,"exampleId":14380,"difficulty":1}},{"id":62260350,"studentId":57975,"choices":null,"selectedChoice":1,"selectId":0,"correct":1,"timeElapsed":12268,"question":{"id":44928,"exampleId":14380,"difficulty":2}}],"completedStr":"Completed @ 12:22 PM","exampleAnswers":[{"id":14378,"number":1,"title":"Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence","answers":[{"id":62260242,"created":"2026-10-15T12:21:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13891,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:21 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":44935,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":14378,"text":"<p>An arithmetic sequence $f(n)$ is defined by </p>\n<p>\\[\nf(n+1) = f(n) - 7,\\quad f(1) = 4,\\quad  n\\geq 1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>What is the $4$th term of the sequence?</p>\n","choice1":"$-17$","choice2":"$-10$","choice3":"$-24$","choice4":"$-14$","choice5":"$-20$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Starting with the first term $f(1)=4,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $4$th term $f(4).$</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\nf(1) &= 4\\\\[3pt]\nf(2) &= f(1) - 7 = 4-7 = -3\\\\[3pt]\nf(3) &= f(2) - 7 = -3-7 = -10 \\\\[3pt]\nf(4) &= f(3) - 7 = -10-7= -17\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the $4$th term is $f(4)=-17.$ </p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14378,"title":"Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"},"group":{"id":79854,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14240563,"answer":{"id":62260242,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:21:41.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13891},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62260270,"created":"2026-10-15T12:21:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[\"75\"]","timeElapsed":10111,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:21 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":215884,"format":"FR","difficulty":3,"exampleId":14378,"text":"An arithmetic sequence $a_n$ is defined by \n\\[a_{n+1} = a_n + 15,\\quad a_1 = 0,\\quad n\\geq 1?\\]\nThe $6$th term of this sequence is ","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":"[\n    answer:75;\n    type: number;\n    width: 25;\n    margin-left: 6;\n    margin-right: 1;\nbuttons: frac;\n].","explanation":"<p>Starting with the first term $a_1=0,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $6$th term $a_6.$\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\na_1 &= 0\\\\[3pt]\na_2 &= a_1 + 15 = 0 + 15 = 15 \\\\[3pt]\na_3 &= a_2 + 15 = 15 + 15 = 30 \\\\[3pt]\na_4 &= a_3 + 15 = 30 + 15 = 45 \\\\[3pt]\na_5 &= a_4 + 15 = 45 + 15 = 60 \\\\[3pt]\na_6 &= a_5 + 15 = 60 + 15 = 75\n\\end{align}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Therefore, the $6$th term is $a_6=\\bbox[4pt,border: 1px solid lightgray]{75}.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14378,"title":"Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"},"group":{"id":79863,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14240563,"answer":{"id":62260270,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:21:57.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":["75"],"timeElapsed":10111},"graphic":false,"freeResponse":{"segments":[{"textbox":{"answer":"75","type":"number","width":25,"margin":{"left":6,"right":1},"buttons":["frac"]}},{"text":"."}]},"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":14380,"number":2,"title":"Finding a Recursive Formula","answers":[{"id":62260317,"created":"2026-10-15T12:22:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15944,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:22 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":67194,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":14380,"text":"<p>What is the recursive formula for the following arithmetic sequence?\n\\[\n-5, \\: -2, \\: 1, \\: \\ldots \n\\]</p>\n","choice1":"$a_{n+1}= a_n +3, \\quad a_1=-5, \\quad n\\geq 1$ ","choice2":"$a_{n+1}= a_n +4, \\quad a_1=-2, \\quad n\\geq 1$  ","choice3":"$a_{n+1}= a_n +2, \\quad a_1=1, \\quad n\\geq 1$  ","choice4":"$a_{n+1}= a_n -5, \\quad a_1=-5, \\quad n\\geq 1$  ","choice5":"$a_{n+1}= a_n -3, \\quad a_1=-5, \\quad n\\geq 1$  ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d$ is</p>\n<p>\\[\na_{n+1} =a_n+d.\n\\]</p>\n<p>In our case, the common difference is</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*} \nd\n&=a_2-a_1 \\\\[3pt]\n&=-2-(-5) \\\\[3pt] \n&=-2+5 \\\\[3pt]\n&=3.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Consequently, the recursive formula for this sequence is</p>\n<p>\\[ \na_{n+1}= a_n +3, \\quad a_1=-5, \\quad n\\geq 1\\,. \n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14380,"title":"Finding a Recursive Formula"},"group":{"id":79870,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14240563,"answer":{"id":62260317,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:22:21.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15944},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62260350,"created":"2026-10-15T12:22:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12268,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 12:22 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":44928,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":14380,"text":"<p>What is the recursive formula for the following arithmetic sequence?\n\\[\n11, \\: 7, \\: 3, \\: \\ldots\n\\]</p>\n","choice1":"$a_{n+1} = a_n - 4,\\quad a_1 = 11,\\quad n\\geq 1$","choice2":"$a_{n+1} = a_n - 4,\\quad a_1 = 1,\\quad n\\geq 1$","choice3":"$a_{n+1} = a_n + 4,\\quad a_1 = 1,\\quad n\\geq 1$","choice4":"$a_{n+1} = a_n + 4,\\quad a_1 = 11,\\quad n\\geq 1$","choice5":"$a_{n+1} = a_n + 11,\\quad a_1 = 1,\\quad n\\geq 1$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d$ is</p>\n<p>\\[\na_{n+1} =a_n+d.\n\\]</p>\n<p>In our case, the common difference is</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*} \nd\n&=a_2-a_1 \\\\[3pt]\n&=7-11 \\\\[3pt]\n&=-4.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Consequently, the recursive formula for this sequence is</p>\n<p>\\[ \na_{n+1}= a_n - 4, \\quad a_1=11, \\quad n\\geq 1\\,.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14380,"title":"Finding a Recursive Formula"},"group":{"id":79874,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14240563,"answer":{"id":62260350,"cread":"2026-10-15T12:22:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12268},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":3695,"topics":[{"id":667,"name":"Arithmetic Sequences","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":1.8753678691057805,"repetition":2,"stability":0.20544076511140094},{"id":1226,"name":"Recursive Sequences","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":3.486787687001481,"repetition":2,"stability":0.25995461418719196},{"id":2214,"name":"Translating Between Explicit and Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences","prerequisites":[3695],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences","prerequisites":[667,1226],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.2793728608313928,"repetition":1,"stability":0.08910992812951057}]}}}